This is the readme for DDR and AXI Verification waveforms
We have created
SELF CHECKING TESTBENCH for DDR and AXI verification
which contains pass variables for different internal conditions

1. DDR -> 
  Waveform verifies that the double-sized data presented to 
  the rising edge is correctly divided and presented onto
  the rising and falling edges of the clock.
  The waveform shows pass details of the color outputs i.e. 
  RED, BLUE and GREEN and the sync outputs i.e.
  HSYNC and VSYNC. 

2. AXI ->
  This waveform shows the verification of myip (custom AXI Peripheral)
  We update data using axi_write (function created in tb_self_check_axi.v)
  The waveform shows pass details of whether the
  block size, speed and color state variables are
  getting duely updated. Additionally, an all_tests_passed variable
  remains high only if all other tests pass.                               
